Molar extinction coefficients (ε) were obtained by measuring absorbance across a range of known concentrations (1–6 μM) in DMSO. Absorbance spectra were acquired using a 10 mm path length quartz cuvette on a UV–vis spectrophotometer. For each concentration point, measurements were repeated in triplicate, and ε values were calculated from the slope of the linear fit of absorbance versus concentration according to the Beer–Lambert law:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
